  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPS - CARITAS V008 CANBERRA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Aotearoa New Zealand (CANZ) is working with design and implementation partner, Tutu Rural Training Centre (TRTC), to achieve mutually identified outcomes of enhanced health and wellbeing, improved gender equality, and stronger, more diverse and climate-resilient livelihoods.  TRTC supports rural training programmes for young farmers, providing students with the skills, opportunities, and tools to run their own small businesses. They train farmers in water and soil management, using resilient seed and seedlings, land and crop stability, and organic pest control and fertilisers. TRTC provides opportunities to support single women and mothers and young people, and teaches agricultural, building and construction methods resistant to climate-amplified storms and weather events.</narrative>
  </description>
